        "source_check": "verified",
        "source_checked_on": "2026-09-05",
        "source_note": "The authors identify run 2 as CaFe2O4-type MgAl2O4 and construct a separate second-order Birch curve by fixing recovered V0, assuming K0'=4, and calculating K0 from one compressed cell. They explicitly state that more points would be needed for a robust modulus and an estimate of K0'.",
        "audit": "../audits/mgal2o4_cafe2o4.audit.json#mgal2o4_cafe2o4_funamori_1998_bm2_1"
      },
      "model": "BM2",
      "parameters": {
        "V0": {"value": 240.3, "error": 0.2, "fixed": true},
        "K0": {"value": 211.0, "error": 6.0}
      },
      "parameter_error_confidence": null,
      "parameter_covariance": null,
      "validity": {
        "pressure_gpa": [0.0, 33.4],
        "notes": [
          "The only nonzero-pressure volume is the in-situ run-2 observation after laser heating; the zero-pressure volume is measured after recovery.",
          "The interval describes the two observations constraining the source parameterization, not a continuous stability field.",
          "K0'=4 is fixed by the second-order Birch finite-strain model.",
          "This is a historical one-point endpoint construction, not a regression EOS; later multi-point studies should be preferred for quantitative compression work."
        ]
      },
      "experimental_pressure_range_gpa": [0.0, 33.4],
      "pressure_range_status": "reported_exactly",
      "determination_method": "experimental",
      "record_kind": "published",
      "notes": "This record describes only the CaFe2O4-type run-2 product. It is distinct from the higher-pressure CaTi2O4-type MgAl2O4 phase in runs 3 and 4. It remains a production published record because the equation, coefficients, construction states, and provenance are complete, but it must not be presented as a multi-point fit.",
      "fit_datasets": ["mgal2o4_cafe2o4_funamori_1998_text_pv"],
      "reference": {
        "authors": ["Funamori", "Jeanloz", "Nguyen", "Kavner", "Caldwell", "Fujino", "Miyajima", "Shinmei", "Tomioka"],
